From 163a198104ccbdf2b99e50272366040044dd4030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:39:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 66/74] Song browser: fewer folder reads next to a large group;
 no delete on a folded row

Next to a group of versions larger than the window of file items, every
encoder step re-read the folder (fillWindowForRows() re-read whenever the
top row was the window's first item, and a read around the selection
left it so), and stepping across the group took 5-6 reads.
Now the rows re-read only when the top file's own row depends on what lies
above the window (it isn't followed by a version of its own group), at most
once per window and side, and the window is read reaching ahead of the
steps over a group (from the row that stays at the top of the screen, or up
to the file after the selection) instead of around the selection. The top
row is kept by name, not by counted index. Next to the group: 0 reads per
step (was 1); across 120 versions: 2-4 (was 4-6).

SHIFT+SAVE on a folded group's row would delete the group's first version,
which the row doesn't show and the prompt doesn't name. It's refused with a
popup ("Open the group first", 7-segment "OPEN"); on a version shown by its
name the prompt opens as before.

